WEBVTT

00:00:00.604 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.639 --> 00:00:05.150
Today, we are talking about spa hand and foot treatments.

00:00:05.462 --> 00:00:07.710
No nail art, no gel polish.

00:00:07.979 --> 00:00:08.669
Instead:

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:14.998
soaking, exfoliating, caring for the skin around the nails, smoothing the heels,

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.510
massage, and a mask,

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:17.310
or paraffin.

00:00:17.739 --> 00:00:18.990
Clients come to rest.

00:00:19.309 --> 00:00:22.813
But the feet are also where fungus and infections spread easily,

00:00:22.763 --> 00:00:24.270
if hygiene is not thorough.

00:00:24.896 --> 00:00:26.196
Something very common:

00:00:26.502 --> 00:00:30.894
the salon is busy, and the foot bath is only drained, given a quick rinse,

00:00:30.844 --> 00:00:32.596
and the next client comes in.

00:00:32.994 --> 00:00:33.956
It looks clean.

00:00:34.483 --> 00:00:37.836
But skin and soap residue stick to the sides of the tub,

00:00:37.786 --> 00:00:40.196
and inside the pipes of a whirlpool tub.

00:00:40.705 --> 00:00:43.236
That is where bacteria and fungi thrive.

00:00:43.666 --> 00:00:46.356
All it takes is a small scratch on a client's foot.

00:00:46.949 --> 00:00:50.355
Spa hand and foot care is quite different from a nail service:

00:00:50.478 --> 00:00:52.675
slow, warm and quiet.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:57.369
Warm towels, warm water, soft music, and little conversation,

00:00:57.319 --> 00:00:59.315
if the client wants to rest.

00:00:59.743 --> 00:01:02.915
But working slowly does not mean skipping any hygiene step.

00:01:03.569 --> 00:01:08.250
For example, the hygiene guidance of the City of Helsinki, in Finland,

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.243
states clearly:

00:01:09.512 --> 00:01:11.323
foot baths must use liners.

00:01:11.646 --> 00:01:15.720
Pedicure tools must always be sterilized, for example in an autoclave,

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:17.963
and stored separately from other tools.

00:01:18.303 --> 00:01:22.123
Rules differ from country to country, so find out the rules where you work.

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:24.610
A liner does not replace cleaning.

00:01:25.011 --> 00:01:26.130
After every client:

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:30.722
throw away the liner, clean the tub with soap and a brush, rinse it,

00:01:30.672 --> 00:01:32.450
and only then disinfect it,

00:01:32.639 --> 00:01:34.290
for the contact time on the bottle.

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:39.010
Cleaning must come first, because dirt makes the disinfectant less effective.

00:01:39.252 --> 00:01:40.875
For a whirlpool tub with pipes,

00:01:40.825 --> 00:01:43.615
do the extra steps in the manufacturer's instructions,

00:01:43.565 --> 00:01:46.050
and clean more thoroughly at the end of the day.

00:01:46.657 --> 00:01:51.423
Before soaking, look closely at the feet and hands, between the toes too.

00:01:51.849 --> 00:01:56.463
Skin between the toes that is white, peeling, cracked, or itchy.

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:59.583
Thick, discolored, crumbly nails.

00:01:59.928 --> 00:02:00.623
Warts.

00:02:00.822 --> 00:02:05.823
Open wounds, and areas that are swollen, red, hot, or painful.

00:02:06.328 --> 00:02:08.943
If you see these signs, don't work on that area;

00:02:09.132 --> 00:02:12.623
sometimes you need to rebook, and advise the client to see a doctor.

00:02:12.968 --> 00:02:14.223
We do not diagnose;

00:02:14.427 --> 00:02:15.823
we only say what we see.

00:02:16.428 --> 00:02:21.422
Clients with diabetes, or poor circulation in the feet, need double the care.

00:02:21.911 --> 00:02:23.902
Their feet may have reduced sensation:

00:02:24.247 --> 00:02:28.142
if the water is too hot, or they get scratched, they may not notice.

00:02:28.489 --> 00:02:31.502
And even a small scratch takes a very long time to heal.

00:02:31.905 --> 00:02:32.382
So:

00:02:32.651 --> 00:02:37.886
the water only lukewarm, test it yourself first, a short soak, no blades,

00:02:37.836 --> 00:02:39.022
no cutting skin,

00:02:39.211 --> 00:02:40.462
and no hot paraffin.

00:02:40.891 --> 00:02:42.702
A foot with an ulcer or a wound:

00:02:42.943 --> 00:02:47.582
don't work on it, and advise the client to see a doctor, or a podiatrist.

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:50.473
Soaking cleans and softens the skin.

00:02:50.877 --> 00:02:52.473
Warm water, not hot:

00:02:52.732 --> 00:02:54.393
test it on your own wrist first.

00:02:54.564 --> 00:02:58.313
Usually just a few minutes, about five to ten, depending on the treatment.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:03.113
Soak too long, and the skin gets soggy, and very easy to over-scrub.

00:03:03.379 --> 00:03:05.513
Soaking salts and essential oils:

00:03:05.623 --> 00:03:07.993
use products made for feet, at the brand's dose.

00:03:08.591 --> 00:03:09.680
Exfoliation:

00:03:09.786 --> 00:03:14.480
fine grains, like sugar or fine salt, rubbed in gentle circles.

00:03:14.907 --> 00:03:18.320
The skin on the feet is thick, so be more thorough on the heels.

00:03:18.756 --> 00:03:22.400
The skin on the hands is much thinner, so use much lighter pressure.

00:03:22.782 --> 00:03:26.880
Do not exfoliate over scratches, cracks, or irritated skin.

00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:28.973
The skin around the nails:

00:03:29.234 --> 00:03:32.333
apply a softening cream, then push back gently.

00:03:32.747 --> 00:03:35.532
The living skin around the nail is a protective barrier;

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:36.333
don't cut it.

00:03:36.678 --> 00:03:40.658
Only trim small bits of dry, loose skin, if you are trained,

00:03:40.608 --> 00:03:42.493
and with sterilized nippers.

00:03:42.842 --> 00:03:45.533
The basic nail care lesson covers this in detail.

00:03:45.802 --> 00:03:47.053
There is no polish here:

00:03:47.082 --> 00:03:49.453
just clean, neat, and nourished.

00:03:50.079 --> 00:03:51.149
Calloused heels:

00:03:51.319 --> 00:03:53.629
the goal is smooth, not removing it all.

00:03:53.888 --> 00:03:55.949
The callus is the foot's protective layer.

00:03:56.218 --> 00:03:58.589
Use a foot file, gently and evenly.

00:03:59.098 --> 00:04:00.749
Callus shavers and blades:

00:04:00.947 --> 00:04:05.069
don't use them, unless the rules where you work, and your training, allow it.

00:04:05.497 --> 00:04:08.269
In many places, that is a job for a podiatrist.

00:04:08.777 --> 00:04:11.229
Deep cracks in the heel that bleed or hurt:

00:04:11.578 --> 00:04:13.309
advise the client to see a doctor.

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:17.164
Hand and foot massage is the part clients remember most.

00:04:17.549 --> 00:04:19.724
Moderate pressure, and ask the client.

00:04:20.213 --> 00:04:24.443
Long strokes from the fingers to the wrist, from the toes to the ankle,

00:04:24.393 --> 00:04:26.444
and up the calf, toward the heart.

00:04:27.031 --> 00:04:29.164
Do not press on varicose veins.

00:04:29.595 --> 00:04:31.084
Clients with diabetes:

00:04:31.188 --> 00:04:32.284
very gently.

00:04:32.793 --> 00:04:37.404
Pressing the sole of the foot to relax is fine, but don't promise to cure anything.

00:04:38.024 --> 00:04:41.255
Masks and paraffin are extras, depending on the treatment.

00:04:41.873 --> 00:04:45.255
Warm paraffin softens the skin, and holds in moisture.

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:49.895
The temperature follows the brand, and always test it on your own wrist first.

00:04:50.243 --> 00:04:51.975
Use it only on intact skin.

00:04:52.475 --> 00:04:53.335
On hygiene:

00:04:53.604 --> 00:04:57.095
never dip the client's hands or feet straight into a shared pot.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:02.615
Take paraffin out into a separate bowl, and brush it on, or use single-client packs.

00:05:02.782 --> 00:05:06.135
Used paraffin is thrown away, never poured back into the pot.

00:05:06.666 --> 00:05:07.491
To finish:

00:05:07.597 --> 00:05:08.851
apply moisturizer.

00:05:09.181 --> 00:05:12.691
Advise the client to moisturize their hands and feet every day.

00:05:12.954 --> 00:05:18.131
Heels with a lot of cracks, or ingrown toenails, are better seen by a podiatrist.

00:05:18.557 --> 00:05:21.971
Write it in the internal notes on the client record in VaraaAi:

00:05:22.319 --> 00:05:26.371
how the skin was, what was done, and the pressure the client likes.

00:05:26.776 --> 00:05:31.091
When the client comes back, check the notes, to see whether the heels have improved.

00:05:31.659 --> 00:05:32.390
Finally:

00:05:32.471 --> 00:05:34.470
rules differ from country to country.

00:05:34.897 --> 00:05:38.230
This lesson is training material, not a professional license.

00:05:38.652 --> 00:05:41.726
In the practice lesson, we will do a spa foot treatment,

00:05:41.676 --> 00:05:43.670
then a hand treatment with paraffin,

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:44.710
step by step.

00:05:45.139 --> 00:05:47.990
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.

00:05:48.243 --> 00:05:49.110
See you next time.
